{"title":"Career Roadmap · UX Researcher","role":"UX Researcher","summary":"A UX Researcher studies users to understand their needs, behaviours, motivations, frustrations and decision-making patterns and converts those findings into evidence that guides product and experience decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"UI/UX & Interaction Design"},"about":[{"label":"Degree–Career Alignment","text":"Excellent"},{"label":"Career Type","text":"User Research + Behaviour + Product + Data"},{"label":"Typical Entry Level","text":"UX Research Intern / Research Assistant / UX Research Associate"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"What Does a UX Researcher Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A UX Researcher studies users to understand their needs, behaviours, motivations, frustrations and decision-making patterns and converts those findings into evidence that guides product and experience decisions."},{"type":"h","text":"UX Researchers commonly work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product designers"},{"text":"UX/UI designers"},{"text":"Product managers"},{"text":"Engineers"},{"text":"Data analysts"},{"text":"Marketing teams"},{"text":"Customer success teams"},{"text":"Business stakeholders"}]},{"type":"h","text":"The core question is:"},{"type":"p","text":"“What do users actually need, why do they behave this way, and what evidence should guide the product decision?”"},{"type":"p","text":"A UX Researcher may investigate a product before it is designed, during prototyping, or after launch."}]},{"heading":"Career Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"During B.Des"},{"text":"UX Research Intern, User Research Intern, Design Research Intern"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"UX Research Associate, Junior UX Researcher, User Research Associate, Research Assistant"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"UX Researcher, Product Researcher, User Researcher"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior UX Researcher, Senior Product Researcher"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Lead UX Researcher, Research Manager, Head of UX Research"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Quantitative UX Researcher, Qualitative UX Researcher, Behavioural Researcher, ResearchOps Specialist, Human-AI Interaction Researcher"}]]}]},{"heading":"What a UX Researcher Actually Does","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"A typical research cycle looks like:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Business/Product Problem","Research Questions","Research Plan","Participant Recruitment","Interviews / Surveys / Observation / Usability Testing","Data Analysis","Insights & Evidence","Recommendations","Design/Product Decisions","Validation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Common research activities"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Examples"],"rows":[[{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"One-to-one interviews"}],[{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Testing prototypes/products"}],[{"text":"Contextual research"},{"text":"Studying users in their environment"}],[{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Large-scale quantitative research"}],[{"text":"Diary studies"},{"text":"Longitudinal behaviour research"}],[{"text":"Card sorting"},{"text":"Information architecture"}],[{"text":"Tree testing"},{"text":"Navigation testing"}],[{"text":"A/B testing"},{"text":"Comparing experiences"}],[{"text":"Competitive research"},{"text":"Studying competing products"}],[{"text":"Journey mapping"},{"text":"Mapping user experience"}],[{"text":"Qualitative analysis"},{"text":"Coding themes and patterns"}],[{"text":"Quantitative analysis"},{"text":"Statistical analysis of user data"}]]}]},{"heading":"Build Skills During B.Des","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — UX & Research Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with understanding users before interfaces."},{"type":"h","text":"Design fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design thinking"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Interaction design"},{"text":"Visual hierarchy"},{"text":"Information architecture"},{"text":"Basic typography"},{"text":"Accessibility fundamentals"},{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Usability principles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"Problem framing"},{"text":"Research questions"},{"text":"User personas"},{"text":"Customer journeys"},{"text":"Basic survey design"},{"text":"Competitive analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"h","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"FigJam"},{"text":"Miro"},{"text":"Google Forms"},{"text":"Excel/Google Sheets"},{"text":"Notion"}]},{"type":"h","text":"First project"},{"type":"h","text":"Student Productivity Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Research:"},{"type":"p","text":"Why do college students struggle to manage assignments, exams and learning resources?"},{"type":"h","text":"Conduct:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"10–15 interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Competitor analysis"},{"text":"Short survey"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"},{"text":"User journey"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Then produce:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research findings","user needs","opportunities"]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not immediately jump into designing an app."}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Research Methods + Psychology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student develops genuine research capability."},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative methods"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Semi-structured interviews"},{"text":"Contextual inquiry"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Diary studies"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative methods"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Mean/median"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Basic regression"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"A/B testing fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"p","text":"UX Research benefits enormously from understanding:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural psychology"},{"text":"Perception"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Cognitive load"},{"text":"Behavioural economics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"A UX Researcher does not need to become a clinical psychologist."},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is understanding human behaviour in product and interaction contexts."}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Professional UX Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Year 3 should focus on becoming employable."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced research"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research planning"},{"text":"Participant recruitment"},{"text":"Screener design"},{"text":"Interview guides"},{"text":"Moderated usability testing"},{"text":"Unmoderated testing"},{"text":"Concept testing"},{"text":"Information architecture research"},{"text":"Card sorting"},{"text":"Tree testing"},{"text":"Diary studies"},{"text":"Longitudinal research"},{"text":"Competitive research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research synthesis"},{"type":"h","text":"Become strong at:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Affinity mapping"},{"text":"Thematic coding"},{"text":"User journey mapping"},{"text":"Experience mapping"},{"text":"Personas"},{"text":"Behavioural segmentation"},{"text":"Jobs-to-be-Done"},{"text":"Opportunity mapping"},{"text":"Research frameworks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative UX"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Survey analytics"},{"text":"Funnel analysis"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Conversion"},{"text":"Task success rate"},{"text":"Completion rate"},{"text":"Error rate"},{"text":"Time on task"},{"text":"SUS"},{"text":"CSAT"},{"text":"NPS"},{"text":"A/B testing"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Industry-Level Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["The final year should focus on real-world research","portfolio","internship."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one or two areas."},{"type":"h","text":"Track A — Product UX Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SaaS"},{"text":"Mobile apps"},{"text":"Web applications"},{"text":"Consumer products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track B — E-commerce UX"},{"type":"h","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product discovery"},{"text":"Search"},{"text":"Checkout"},{"text":"Payments"},{"text":"Cart abandonment"},{"text":"Reviews"},{"text":"Personalisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track C — FinTech UX"},{"type":"h","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Payments"},{"text":"Banking"},{"text":"Investment"},{"text":"Financial literacy"},{"text":"Trust"},{"text":"Fraud warnings"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track D — HealthTech UX"},{"type":"h","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient journeys"},{"text":"Healthcare applications"},{"text":"Appointment systems"},{"text":"Medical information"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track E — AI Product Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI assistants"},{"text":"Chatbots"},{"text":"Generative AI interfaces"},{"text":"Human-AI collaboration"},{"text":"Trust in AI"},{"text":"Explainability"},{"text":"AI errors"},{"text":"AI adoption"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is likely to become one of the most valuable UX research specialisations."}]},{"heading":"Four-Year Development Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Focus","Expected Output"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"UX + observation"},{"text":"2–3 mini studies"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Interviews + surveys + psychology"},{"text":"2 major research projects"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Advanced qualitative + quantitative research"},{"text":"2–3 professional case studies"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Specialisation + internship"},{"text":"Portfolio + industry project"}],[{"text":"Graduation"},{"text":"Job readiness"},{"text":"4–6 excellent UX research case studies"}]]}]},{"heading":"UX Research Portfolio","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A UX Research portfolio should not simply show beautiful UI screens."},{"type":"h","text":"It should demonstrate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research problem","Method","Evidence","Analysis","Insight","Product implication"]},{"type":"note","label":"Recommended portfolio","text":"4–6 case studies"},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 1 — User Interview Study"},{"type":"h","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Why do students abandon online learning platforms?"},{"type":"h","text":"Show:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research objective"},{"text":"Research questions"},{"text":"Participant criteria"},{"text":"Screener"},{"text":"Interview guide"},{"text":"Interview findings"},{"text":"Affinity map"},{"text":"Themes"},{"text":"Insights"},{"text":"Recommendations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 2 — Usability Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Test an existing website or application."},{"type":"h","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research objective"},{"text":"Tasks"},{"text":"Participants"},{"text":"Task completion"},{"text":"Errors"},{"text":"Observations"},{"text":"Severity"},{"text":"Usability problems"},{"text":"Recommendations"},{"text":"Retest"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 3 — Quantitative UX Study"},{"type":"h","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"What factors influence users when selecting an online course?"},{"type":"h","text":"Use:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"150–300 survey responses"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Cross-tabulation"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Visualisations"},{"text":"User segments"},{"text":"Conclusions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","Power BI","Python/R"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 4 — Mobile App Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Research an existing application."},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Onboarding"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Search"},{"text":"Task completion"},{"text":"Notifications"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Trust"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then provide evidence-backed recommendations."},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 5 — AI Product Research"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong future-oriented project."},{"type":"h","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"How do students trust and evaluate AI-generated answers?"},{"type":"h","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trust"},{"text":"Accuracy perception"},{"text":"Explainability"},{"text":"Hallucination awareness"},{"text":"User expectations"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates awareness of the emerging AI UX Research field."}]},{"heading":"Tools to Learn","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Tool","Purpose","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Prototypes/interfaces"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"FigJam"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Miro"},{"text":"Collaboration/research"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Google Forms"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Analysis"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Dashboards"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Product data"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Research analytics"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}],[{"text":"R"},{"text":"Statistical research"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Dovetail / similar research repositories"},{"text":"Qualitative analysis"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Maze / similar usability platforms"},{"text":"Testing"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"GA4 / product analytics tools"},{"text":"Behaviour analytics"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Notion/Airtable"},{"text":"Research repository"},{"text":"Intermediate"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact commercial tool used by an employer will vary, so research methodology is more important than memorising a particular platform."}]},{"heading":"Technical Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest modern UX Researcher combines:"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Qualitative analysis"},{"text":"Quantitative analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Information architecture"},{"text":"Interaction design"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Product analytics"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Python/R"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Behaviour"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural science"},{"text":"Consumer psychology"},{"text":"Human factors"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Communication"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research reports"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Stakeholder communication"}]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Start applying for internships from Year 2, with stronger emphasis in Year 3."},{"type":"h","text":"Target organisations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Technology companies"},{"text":"SaaS companies"},{"text":"FinTech companies"},{"text":"E-commerce companies"},{"text":"HealthTech companies"},{"text":"EdTech companies"},{"text":"UX agencies"},{"text":"Design consultancies"},{"text":"Product startups"},{"text":"Research organisations"},{"text":"Consumer brands"},{"text":"Banks and digital financial services"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Search for these titles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"User Research Intern"},{"text":"Product Research Intern"},{"text":"Design Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"UX Research Associate Intern"},{"text":"Consumer Research Intern"},{"text":"Human Factors Research Intern"},{"text":"Product Design Research Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target before graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"2 internships + 1 live product research project is a strong minimum target."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certificates should support the portfolio rather than replace it."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended learning areas"},{"type":"h","text":"UX Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User Research"},{"text":"Usability Testing"},{"text":"UX Research Methods"},{"text":"Human-Centred Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"Information Architecture"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Python/R"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Behaviour"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive Psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Human Factors"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Product"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product Management fundamentals"},{"text":"Product analytics"},{"text":"A/B testing"},{"text":"Experimentation"}]}]},{"heading":"Jobs After Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Direct-entry roles"},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Alignment"],"rows":[[{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"UX Research Assistant"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"UX Research Associate"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Junior UX Researcher"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"User Research Associate"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Product Research Associate"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Design Research Associate"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Research Analyst – UX"},{"text":"Very Good"}],[{"text":"Consumer Research Associate"},{"text":"Good"}],[{"text":"Human Factors Research Assistant"},{"text":"Good"}],[{"text":"Product Insights Associate"},{"text":"Very Good"}],[{"text":"Research Operations Associate"},{"text":"Good"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Important"},{"type":"p","text":"Some companies use “UX Researcher” only for candidates with previous research experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, do not restrict the job search to one title."},{"type":"h","text":"Search across:"},{"type":"flow","items":["UX Research","User Research","Product Research","Design Research","Product Insights","Research Associate."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"After 2–5 Years","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Possible progression:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX Researcher"},{"text":"Product Researcher"},{"text":"User Researcher"},{"text":"Qualitative UX Researcher"},{"text":"Quantitative UX Researcher"},{"text":"Consumer Insights Researcher"},{"text":"Service Design Researcher"},{"text":"Behavioural Researcher"},{"text":"Human Factors Researcher"}]}]},{"heading":"Senior Career","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"With substantial experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior UX Researcher"},{"text":"Senior Product Researcher"},{"text":"Lead UX Researcher"},{"text":"UX Research Lead"},{"text":"Research Manager"},{"text":"Design Research Lead"},{"text":"Research Operations Lead"},{"text":"Head of UX Research"},{"text":"Director of User Research"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Options in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A master's degree is not mandatory for becoming a UX Researcher, but it can help for research-intensive or specialist careers."},{"type":"table","header":["PG","Best For"],"rows":[[{"text":"M.Des UX/HCI"},{"text":"Advanced UX research"}],[{"text":"M.Des Interaction Design"},{"text":"Interaction research"}],[{"text":"M.Des Design Research"},{"text":"Design research"}],[{"text":"MSc/MDes Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"HCI research"}],[{"text":"MSc Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Behaviour + cognition"}],[{"text":"MSc Psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural research"}],[{"text":"MSc Human Factors"},{"text":"Human-product interaction"}],[{"text":"MA/MSc Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Behavioural research"}],[{"text":"MBA Product Management"},{"text":"Product strategy"}],[{"text":"MBA Marketing"},{"text":"Consumer research"}],[{"text":"MSc Data Analytics"},{"text":"Quantitative UX"}],[{"text":"MA/Design Studies"},{"text":"Research/theory"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For academic research or highly specialised human-computer interaction research, a master's and potentially PhD can become valuable."}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. Qualitative UX Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Interviews","observation","behavioural insights"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Best for people who enjoy:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conversations"},{"text":"Human behaviour"},{"text":"Ethnography"},{"text":"Storytelling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Quantitative UX Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Data","experiments","statistics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Python/R"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Experimentation"},{"text":"Product analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a particularly strong combination with a data-oriented skill set."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Product Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User needs","product strategy","business outcomes"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Works closely with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product managers"},{"text":"Designers"},{"text":"Engineering"},{"text":"Business teams"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Human Factors Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"h","text":"Human capabilities + technology/product interaction"},{"type":"h","text":"Important in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Automotive"},{"text":"Aerospace"},{"text":"Industrial systems"},{"text":"Safety-critical products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Service Design Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"p","text":"Entire customer journey rather than one interface."},{"type":"h","text":"Useful in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Banking"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Government"},{"text":"Travel"},{"text":"Retail"},{"text":"Telecom"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Consumer Insights Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"h","text":"Consumer behaviour + market decisions"},{"type":"h","text":"Combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["UX","Marketing","Psychology","Data"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"7. AI UX Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging high-value area:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Humans","AI systems","interaction","trust","behaviour"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Potential research areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI trust"},{"text":"Explainability"},{"text":"Human oversight"},{"text":"AI hallucinations"},{"text":"Prompt interaction"},{"text":"AI adoption"},{"text":"Human-AI collaboration"},{"text":"AI accessibility"},{"text":"Agentic AI interfaces"}]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant international master's fields include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"Design Research"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Service Design"},{"text":"Information Science"},{"text":"Product Design"},{"text":"Human-AI Interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Countries worth exploring include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Denmark"},{"text":"Finland"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Australia"}]},{"type":"h","text":"When comparing programmes, prioritise:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research labs"},{"text":"Faculty expertise"},{"text":"Industry projects"},{"text":"Internship opportunities"},{"text":"HCI/UX research curriculum"},{"text":"Graduate employment"},{"text":"Portfolio/research requirements"}]}]},{"heading":"AI-Era UX Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will significantly change UX research workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"AI can assist with"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview transcription"},{"text":"Note organisation"},{"text":"Initial coding"},{"text":"Theme discovery"},{"text":"Survey analysis"},{"text":"Research repository search"},{"text":"Competitor research"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Persona drafting"},{"text":"Sentiment analysis"},{"text":"Behaviour pattern detection"},{"text":"Research report drafting"},{"text":"Research participant screening"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But AI-generated research findings should not automatically be treated as evidence."},{"type":"h","text":"The researcher remains responsible for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research design"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Participant consent"},{"text":"Bias detection"},{"text":"Evidence validation"},{"text":"Context interpretation"},{"text":"Ethical handling of user data"},{"text":"Final conclusions"}]}]},{"heading":"Future UX Research Roles","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By 2030–2045, new combinations are likely to become increasingly relevant:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI UX Researcher"},{"text":"Human-AI Interaction Researcher"},{"text":"AI Product Researcher"},{"text":"Behavioural AI Researcher"},{"text":"Conversational UX Researcher"},{"text":"Research Intelligence Specialist"},{"text":"Research Operations Lead"},{"text":"AI Experience Strategist"},{"text":"Human Factors & AI Researcher"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile will increasingly combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["UX Research","Behavioural Science","Product Analytics","AI","Product Strategy"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"B.Des UI/UX & Interaction Design"},{"type":"h","text":"UX Research Intern"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Assistant /"},{"type":"h","text":"UX Research Associate"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior UX Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"UX Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior UX Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Lead UX Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Head of UX Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative paths:"},{"type":"h","text":"UX Research"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"┌───────────────┼────────────────┐"},{"type":"h","text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"type":"h","text":"Product Research Quant UX Qual UX Research"},{"type":"h","text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"type":"h","text":"Product Strategy Data/Analytics Behavioural Research"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Service Design"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Human Factors"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Consumer Insights"},{"type":"h","text":"└── Human-AI Interaction"}]},{"heading":"Ideal Graduate Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"By graduation, the student should have:"},{"type":"h","text":"UX Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Contextual inquiry"},{"text":"Diary studies"},{"text":"Card sorting"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural science"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Cognitive load"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Basic Python/R"},{"text":"Product analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Information architecture"},{"text":"Interaction design"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"4–6 strong case studies, ideally including:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"1 interview study"},{"text":"1 usability study"},{"text":"1 quantitative study"},{"text":"1 product research study"},{"text":"1 AI/Human-AI research study"},{"text":"1 live industry project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Experience"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"2 internships"},{"text":"1 live product project"},{"text":"Research presentation experience"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Practical Path"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des UI/UX & Interaction Design","Learn Human-Centred Design + Psychology","Master Interviews + Observation + Usability Testing","Learn Survey Design + Statistics","Build Figma + Excel + Power BI + SQL skills","Add Product Analytics + Python/R","Complete 4–6 strong UX Research case studies","Do 2 internships + 1 live product research project","Apply for UX Research Associate / User Research Associate / Product Research Associate roles","Become UX Researcher","Specialise in Product / Quantitative / Qualitative / Behavioural / Human Factors / AI UX Research","Senior UX Researcher → Lead → Research Manager → Head of UX Research"]},{"type":"note","label":"Overall Assessment","text":"Excellent"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Des in UI/UX & Interaction Design is one of the strongest undergraduate foundations for UX Research. The key differentiator is to avoid becoming only a UI designer. Build deep capability in research methodology, psychology, statistics, product analytics and evidence-based decision-making. That combination creates a much stronger UX Research profile for the AI-era product industry."}]}]}